          "content": {
            "size": 2762,
            "mimeType": "application/javascript",
            "text": "const e={name:\"DKS (Dynamic Keystroke)\",menu_desc:\"Up to four actions from a single key based on press/release depth\",desc:\"Each keystroke is divided into four positions—actuation, bottom-out, release from bottom-out, and full release. You can assign 1–4 actions to these positions.\",guide:\"Choose an action from the list and bind it to a position. For a one-time trigger, click the “+” icon. For a sustained hold, click the “+” icon and drag it across additional “+” icons.\"},t={name:\"MT (Tap/Hold Dual-Action)\",menu_desc:\"Tap or hold to execute different actions\",desc:\"One key, two actions: a tap performs Action A, a hold performs Action B.\",guide:\"One key, two actions: a tap performs Action A, a hold performs Action B.\"},o={name:\"TGL (Toggle)\",menu_desc:\"Single tap toggles auto-repeat; hold behaves normally\",desc:\"Tap once to start or stop continuous input; hold acts as a standard press.\",guide:\"Tap once to start or stop continuous input; hold acts as a standard press.\"},s={name:\"MPT (Multi-Point Trigger)\",menu_desc:\"Three actions based on press depth\",desc:\"A single key can trigger three different actions at three press depths.\",guide:\"A single key can trigger three different actions at three press depths.\"},n={name:\"END (Release Trigger)\",menu_desc:\"Press triggers Action A; release may trigger Action B based on hold time\",desc:\"Press triggers Action A; release may trigger Action B depending on how long the key was held.\",guide:\"Press triggers Action A; release may trigger Action B depending on how long the key was held.\"},r={name:\"SOCD (Dual-Key Trigger)\",menu_desc:\"Monitors two keys and resolves input based on your rule\",desc:\"Continuously monitors two keys and triggers according to your chosen rule.\",guide:`Continuously monitors two keys and triggers according to your rule.\nLast Input Priority: the most recent key overrides the previous.\nNeutral: pressing both keys sends neither.\nKey 1 Priority: Key 1 always overrides Key 2.\nKey 2 Priority: Key 2 always overrides Key 1.`},i={name:\"AT (Alternating Trigger)\",menu_desc:\"When two keys are held, outputs alternate between them\",desc:\"Outputs alternate between two keys when they are pressed simultaneously.\",guide:\"Outputs alternate between two keys when they are pressed simultaneously.\"},a={name:\"RS (RS)\",menu_desc:\"Monitors two keys, fires the deeper key; if both bottom out, fires both\",desc:\"Continuously monitors two keys, triggering the one pressed deeper; if both bottom out, both are triggered.\",guide:\"Continuously monitors two keys, triggering the one pressed deeper; if both bottom out, both are triggered.\"},d={DKS:e,MT:t,TGL:o,MPT:s,END:n,SOCD:r,AT:i,RS:a};export{i as AT,e as DKS,n as END,s as MPT,t as MT,a as RS,r as SOCD,o as TGL,d as default};\n"
          },
          "redirectURL": "",
